# About NE Fiber

NE Fiber is the broadband initiative of the North East Mississippi Electric Power Association (NEMEPA). Since 1942, NEMEPA has served the people of Northeast Mississippi with safe, affordable, and reliable electricity. In 2020, NEMEPA recognized the growing need for broadband connectivity in our communities and created NE Fiber to bridge the digital divide.

Our mission is to deliver fast, reliable, and affordable internet to rural communities in Northeast Mississippi, ensuring residents and businesses have the bandwidth they need to thrive in today's connected world.

## Our Technology

NE Fiber uses fiber optic technology to provide the highest quality internet service available. Our fiber network provides:

* **Speeds up to 1 Gbps for residential customers**
* **Speeds up to 10 Gbps for business customers**
* **Symmetrical download and upload speeds**
* **No data caps**
* **Interference-free service**

## Our Service Area

NE Fiber is currently providing service to members in the following counties: Prentiss, Tishomingo, Alcorn, Tippah, and Union Counties. We are actively expanding our network to serve more members across Northeast Mississippi.

## Our Parent Organization

The North East Mississippi Electric Power Association (NEMEPA) is a non-profit electric cooperative. We are proud to serve our members across 9 counties in Northeast Mississippi. NEMEPA is a Touchstone Energy Cooperative and is a member of the Mississippi Association of Electric Cooperatives.

## Our Team

NE Fiber is operated by a dedicated team of professionals committed to providing the best internet service possible. Our team includes experts in network engineering, customer service, and fiber optic technology.

