# BEAD Program Overview

## Mississippi BEAD Program

The Mississippi Broadband Expansion & Access for Deployment (BEAD) Program is being administered by the Mississippi Department of Finance and Administration (DFA). The mission of the BEAD program is to provide reliable, affordable, and high-speed internet service in Mississippi.

Mississippi has been awarded **$1,060,574,537 in BEAD** funds. The program will utilize these funds to expand broadband access to unserved and underserved locations across the state.

### Current Status

**Initial Subgrantee Selections - December 2024**

The following organizations have been selected as initial BEAD subgrantees and are currently in the contracting phase:

* Comcast Cable Communications, LLC
* Delta Telephone Company of Mississippi, Inc.
* Home Telephone Company
* MPower Communications, Inc.
* **North East Mississippi Electric Power Association (NEMEPA)**
* Pine Belt Telephone Company
* Pioneer Telephone Company
* South Central Telephone Association, Inc.
* Southwest Mississippi Electric Power Association
* TeleCove Operations, LLC
* Tombigbee Electric Power Association
* Tombigbee Fiber, Inc.

### Subgrantee Award Amounts

Award amounts for individual subgrantees have not been publicly disclosed at this time. The DFA continues to work with subgrantees to finalize contracts.

### Program Timeline

* **Initial Proposal Approved**: 2024
* **Subgrantee Applications**: Fall 2024
* **Initial Subgrantee Selections**: December 2024
* **Contracting Phase**: Currently ongoing
* **Deployment**: To begin following contract execution

For more information, visit [broadband4ms.ms.gov](https://broadband4ms.ms.gov/).

